event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/plan.md\", \"content\": \"# Plan for mission \\\"greet, tested\\\"\\n\\n1. Dispatch to dev: implement src/greet.py with greet(name) -\u003e \\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\",\\n   and tests/test_greet.py covering a normal name and the empty string. Require\\n   dev to run `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` itself and report the\\n   exit status, then commit to its own branch.\\n2. Judge dev's reply by fetching dev's branch (not trusting the report):\\n   - src/greet.py exists and greet() returns exactly \\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\" for a\\n     normal name and for \\\"\\\" (i.e. \\\"Hello, !\\\").\\n   - tests/test_greet.py exists and actually exercises both cases.\\n   - Run `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself against the fetched\\n     tree and confirm exit code 0.\\n3. If any criterion fails, send precise rework describing exactly what is\\n   wrong. Accept only when all three hold.\\n4. Once accepted, reply to mission m1 with outcome campaign-met (or the\\n   appropriate other outcome if the mission stalls or proves impossible).\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

